<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Old Feuds Have Now Returned, 2014</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;The timeline has diverged, and instead of a vote for unity, the Scottish voted for independence. This was due to many factors-in this timeline, the vote was held earlier, with the combination of the memories of Westminster cuts being more recent and a spike in oil prices making the SNP's platform seem more realistic. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;No sooner had Scotland voted for independence then the troubles began. The rise in oil prices was just an illusion, a&amp;nbsp;short one driven by jitters after the Oman-Pakistan war rather than any serious change in supply and demand. Both countries sank after the messy, calamatous split. The pro-UK Shetland Islands held a referendum of their own, and since maritime boundaries determined who could control the resources, this was a problem. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Warships were sent, the first shots were fired, and wars between&amp;nbsp;the English and Scots have come back. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;-Scenario by Coiler12&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
